  "body": "## What changed (Part 2 of 2)\n\nAdds the RTK management surfaces, all driving the same `~/.fcc/rtk.json` + `apply_rtk_state` reconciler from v5.20.0.\n\n- **Admin API**: `GET /admin/api/rtk` (status + state) and `POST /admin/api/rtk` (persist + reconcile — RTK is machine-global, so it reconciles unlike the persist-only desktop prefs).\n- **Dashboard**: a \"Token optimizer\" card (three toggles + status line) bound to the new endpoints.\n- **Desktop tray**: a \"Token optimizer\" submenu with three checkable items (Claude Code / Codex / Pi).\n\nCLI, dashboard, and tray all converge on one reconciler, so a toggle anywhere is reflected everywhere.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 12 new tests; full suite **4061 passed / 6 failed** (6 = pre-existing PowerShell-installer baseline).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: clean.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Dashboard toggles and tray menu weren't driven against a live pystray backend or real browser (no DOM harness in the suite); the reconciler call is asserted via monkeypatch. Binary download/verify paths are already covered in `tests/config/test_rtk.py`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
